{
  "courseSlug": "understanding-startup-equity-valuation-and-cap-tables-for-investors",
  "chapters": [
    {
      "title": "Chapter 3: Reading and Building a Cap Table",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "title": "Building a Simple Cap Table Round by Round",
          "slug": "building-a-simple-cap-table-round-by-round",
          "body": [
            {
              "_key": "k1",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k2",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Reading a cap table tells you where a company stands. Building one tells you how it got there and where your stake is heading. The good news: every priced round uses the same five steps, and once you can do them for one round you can do them for ten. In this lesson you will build a startup's cap table from incorporation to Series A, one round at a time, and see exactly what happens to every holder along the way.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_type": "bigIdea",
              "text": "A cap table is built one round at a time using the same five steps: start from the fully diluted share count, set the price, issue new shares, add them to the total, and recalculate everyone's percentage.",
              "_key": "k3"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k4",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k5",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The Five-Step Recipe for Any Priced Round",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": []
            },
            {
              "_key": "k6",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k7",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Start from the fully diluted share count",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k8",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " before the round, including any ESOP pool and warrants.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "number",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k9",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k10",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Set the price per share:",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k11",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " pre-money valuation ÷ fully diluted shares before the round.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "number",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k12",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k13",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Calculate new shares:",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k14",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " investment ÷ price per share.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "number",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k15",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k16",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Add a row",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k17",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " for the new investor and update the total share count.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "number",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_key": "k18",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "k19",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Recalculate every holder's percentage",
                  "marks": [
                    "strong"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "_key": "k20",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": " and run the sanity check below.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ],
              "markDefs": [],
              "listItem": "number",
              "level": 1
            },
            {
              "_type": "mathBlock",
              "latex": "\\frac{\\text{New investor's shares}}{\\text{Post-round total shares}} = \\frac{\\text{Investment}}{\\text{Post-money valuation}}",
              "caption": "The sanity check: if these two numbers differ, something in your cap table is wrong",
              "_key": "k21"
            },
            {
              "_key": "k22",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "children": [
