              "unit": "%",
              "explanation": "The Series B investor takes ₹40 crore ÷ ₹160 crore = 25%, so every existing holder keeps 75% of their previous stake. More precisely, 6,00,000 ÷ 17,75,000 = 33.803%, and 33.803% × 0.75 = 25.35%.",
